WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.925
Start on your Windows computer or Mac. Open the YAIP website, choose Download,
then Samsung. Open the Samsung setup guide.

00:00:11.355 --> 00:00:14.930
Keep it nearby so you can pause and follow each step.

00:00:15.511 --> 00:00:24.218
Samsung requires test apps to be signed for each television. First, you will
download a small kit that reads your TV’s unique ID.

00:00:25.229 --> 00:00:31.626
After registration, the bot will send a different kit that can install YAIP on
your TV.

00:00:32.357 --> 00:00:38.488
In the guide, click Download Samsung TV ID kit. Save the ZIP on your computer.

00:00:39.347 --> 00:00:43.387
If you are reading on your phone, open the guide on the computer before
continuing.

00:00:44.293 --> 00:00:57.539
On Windows, open Downloads. Right-click the ZIP, choose Extract All, then
Extract. Open the new folder. Do not run the installer from inside the ZIP.

00:00:57.818 --> 00:01:08.999
On Mac, open Downloads and double-click the ZIP to unpack it. Then open the
new folder. If your browser already unpacked the download, use that folder.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:17.834
Keep all the extracted files together, including the folder named files. Next,
open the installer for your computer.

00:01:18.217 --> 00:01:22.222
You do not need Samsung’s developer tools or a developer account.

00:01:23.035 --> 00:01:33.229
If you use Windows, double-click the Windows installer highlighted on screen.
Its filename is Install on Windows, ending in dot C M D.

00:01:33.542 --> 00:01:41.205
If you use Mac, double-click Install on Mac dot command. Choose only the
installer that matches your computer.

00:01:41.623 --> 00:01:48.357
If Windows blocks this official YAIP kit, choose More info, then Run anyway if
offered.

00:01:49.018 --> 00:01:57.633
If asked, allow Samsung’s connection tool on your private home network. Do not
turn off Windows protection or the firewall.

00:01:58.237 --> 00:02:06.608
If Mac blocks the installer because its developer is unidentified, open System
Settings, then Privacy and Security.

00:02:07.548 --> 00:02:18.206
Find the installer message, choose Open Anyway, and confirm. On Apple silicon,
follow any Rosetta prompt. Never send your Mac password to the bot.

00:02:18.473 --> 00:02:29.363
Make sure the computer and TV are on the same home network, with internet
access. Avoid guest Wi-Fi. A VPN may prevent the devices from seeing each
other.

00:02:29.746 --> 00:02:38.303
A text window opens. This is the installer. Find the line showing this
computer’s IP address and leave the window open.

00:02:38.999 --> 00:02:42.111
You will enter that computer address on the television next.

00:02:42.738 --> 00:02:48.926
On the TV, press Home and open Apps. On some newer models, open App Settings
inside Apps.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:54.475
Menu names can vary, so use the written guide if your screen looks different.

00:02:55.207 --> 00:03:06.782
Enter one, two, three, four, five using the remote’s number buttons or its
on-screen number keypad. The Developer Mode window should appear.

00:03:07.281 --> 00:03:16.128
In that window, turn Developer mode on. This is a built-in Samsung setting.
You do not need to install a separate Developer Mode app.

00:03:16.824 --> 00:03:28.852
In Host PC IP, enter the computer’s IP address shown by the installer, then
confirm. Use your own computer’s address, not the example in this video.

00:03:29.456 --> 00:03:32.243
Do not enter the TV’s address in this field.

00:03:32.684 --> 00:03:44.155
Restart the television as described in the kit. Switch it off, unplug it for
thirty seconds, then reconnect it and turn it on. Keep Developer Mode enabled.

00:03:44.538 --> 00:03:54.696
Find the TV’s own IP address in its network settings, under Network Status and
IP Settings. This is a different address from the computer’s.

00:03:54.871 --> 00:04:00.385
The computer address goes on the TV; the TV address goes into the installer.

00:04:00.896 --> 00:04:11.879
Return to the installer on your computer. When it asks for the TV IP address,
type the address from your television, including the dots, and press Enter.

00:04:12.947 --> 00:04:15.652
The installer will read the TV’s ID.

00:04:15.966 --> 00:04:26.461
Wait for Your TV ID. The complete ID is copied to the clipboard and saved in
the text file shown on screen, inside the extracted folder.

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:35.888
Keep any version prefix. Use this ID, not a serial number or MAC address. This
first kit does not install YAIP.

00:04:36.631 --> 00:04:46.720
Back in the guide, choose Register my TV on Telegram. Open the bot and press
Start if asked, or send the slash Samsung command shown on screen.

00:04:47.417 --> 00:04:56.183
Paste only your complete TV ID and send it. Wait for the bot to confirm that
it is saved. No password is needed.

00:04:57.135 --> 00:05:04.402
Samsung includes TV IDs in the downloadable test certificate and kit, while
your Telegram account stays private.

00:05:04.727 --> 00:05:15.280
Your registration is now saved. The developer starts signing batches, so the
install kit is not ready immediately and there is no fixed waiting time.

00:05:15.791 --> 00:05:20.772
Keep the bot chat available. You can check your status with the same command.

00:05:21.213 --> 00:05:30.199
Later, the bot will tell you when a verified install kit includes your TV.
Download the ZIP from that message on your computer.

00:05:31.012 --> 00:05:36.375
Use your own bot link, because another tester’s kit may not include your
television.

00:05:36.851 --> 00:05:48.554
Extract this new ZIP into a new folder and keep all its files together. Read
Read Me First, then open the Windows or Mac installer again.

00:05:49.042 --> 00:05:53.488
Make sure you are running the new signed kit, not the old ID kit.

00:05:53.999 --> 00:06:03.182
Keep Developer Mode on and check that Host PC IP still matches your computer.
Enter the television’s current IP address in the installer.

00:06:03.566 --> 00:06:12.250
This kit includes your TV, so it transfers and installs YAIP. Leave the
television on and wait for completion.

00:06:12.947 --> 00:06:23.616
YAIP should open on the TV. Later, open it from Apps and add your own
playlist. YAIP is a free player and includes no content.

00:06:24.139 --> 00:06:30.582
For an update, run a newer kit supplied for your TV. Keep the existing app to
preserve local profiles.

00:06:31.279 --> 00:06:41.844
If you get stuck, return to the written guide or ask the support bot. Tell it
your TV model, computer system, the step and the error.

00:06:42.785 --> 00:06:49.553
Hide passwords and TV IDs in screenshots. Pause this video whenever you need
more time.
